{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve.curve_palindromic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve.curve_palindromic","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoSaddleCurve.lean#L71-L79","doc":"x ↔ x⁻¹ palindromy, divisor-free: whenever `x·z = 1`,\n`x²·curve z y = curve x y` — the algebraic face of the u-EVENNESS of the\n5₂ potential (231): the curve is achiral; the chirality of 5₂ (CS ≠ 0)\nlives in the complex saddle values, not in the curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve.curve_pair_certificate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve.curve_pair_certificate","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoSaddleCurve.lean#L59-L69","doc":"Pairwise saddle certificate (the 5₂ analogue of the 4₁ Vieta\ncertificates): `(y₁ − y₂)·(x·(y₁²+y₁y₂+y₂²) − (x²+1)·(y₁+y₂) +\n(x²+x+1)) = curve x y₁ − curve x y₂`. Two distinct on-curve saddles\n(with `y₁ − y₂` a nonzerodivisor) force the second factor to vanish —\nthe relation feeding the exact pairwise singularities\n`ι̃_ij = (V_i − V_j)/(2πi)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve.u0_cubic_discriminant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve.u0_cubic_discriminant","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoSaddleCurve.lean#L51-L57","doc":"The discriminant of the u = 0 saddle cubic `y³ − 2y² + 3y − 1` is\n`−23` — the printed trace-field discriminant of the 5₂ knot. (Cubic\n`ay³+by²+cy+d` with `a=1, b=−2, c=3, d=−1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve.curve_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve.curve_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoSaddleCurve.lean#L45-L49","doc":"At `x = 1` the curve reduces to the printed u = 0 saddle cubic (73):\n`y³ − 2y² + 3y − 1` (equivalently `(1−y)³ = y²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve.curve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoSaddleCurve.curve","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoSaddleCurve.lean#L40-L43","doc":"The cleared deformed 5₂ saddle curve\n`x·y³ − (x²+1)·y² + (x²+x+1)·y − x` (vanishing exactly on the curve). ","signatureChunk":0}]}